// GAP (2026-08-10): cross-thread data race via a CALLER-supplied funcptr
// forwarded to spawn. `run` forwards its funcptr PARAM to a spawn target; the
// data-race scan is intra-function/callee-only and never sees the caller's
// `run(bump)`. Direct sibling `spawn worker(bump)` IS rejected. compile-clean =
// the race is accepted. See limitations.md 2026-08-10.
u32 g;
void bump() { g += 1; }
void worker(*() -> void fp) { fp(); }
void run(*() -> void fp) { spawn worker(fp); }
void main() { run(bump); }
